Source Partial Custom component .agent/template/demo.mdx<pre><code>---
template:
  vars:
    project: the checkout service
    retries: 3
    timeout: 120s
    max_subagents: 3
    checks: [unit tests, lint, security scan]
    surface: terminal
name: demo
description: Demonstrates every template feature by walking through shipping a feature, with questions, subagents, retries and a live status section. Use when the user asks to see the demo template or how the template features work.
compatibility: Works in any harness that reads skills. These are instructions to the model, not technical limits.
metadata:
  version: "1.0.0"
  aiculator.kind: demo
---

{# A Jinja2 comment. It does not reach the rendered skill. #}
{% macro check_row(name, n) %}{{ n }}. Run {{ name }}, and stop if it fails.{% endmacro %}

# Ship a feature in {{ project }}

&lt;Toc depth="2" /&gt;

{# A condition: this differs per harness when rendered with --per-harness. #}
{% if harness.question_tool %}
Rendered for {{ harness.name }}, whose question tool is `{{ harness.question_tool }}`.
{% else %}
Rendered for {{ harness.name }}, so the questions below fall back to numbered lists where needed.
{% endif %}

&lt;Directive id="ship-safely"&gt;Never push to the main branch. Every change goes through a review.&lt;/Directive&gt;

&lt;Directive level="must not" id="no-false-claims"&gt;Say something works unless you ran it and saw it work.&lt;/Directive&gt;

&lt;Note&gt;This skill is a demo of the template features, built around a realistic workflow.&lt;/Note&gt;

{# An include: shared text kept in one file, partials/house-style.md. #}
{% include "partials/house-style.md" %}

&lt;DemoBadge label="Custom component"&gt;This one comes from `components/DemoBadge.md`, next to this template.&lt;/DemoBadge&gt;

&lt;TodoList id="track-work" title="Track the work"&gt;
- Settle the details with the user
- Get the plan approved
- Build and review it
- Open the pull request
&lt;/TodoList&gt;

&lt;AskText id="name-feature" title="Step A: name the feature" question="What should this feature's flag and branch be called?" placeholder="faster-checkout" /&gt;

&lt;AskOne id="choose-approach" title="Step B: choose an approach" question="How should I build this feature?" subagent="Use the smallest change that works, and say so in your report."&gt;
- Smallest change (Recommended): touch as little as possible
- Refactor first: clean the area up, then add the feature
- Feature flag: ship it switched off
&lt;/AskOne&gt;

&lt;AskPreview id="choose-api" title="Step C: choose the API style" question="Which API style reads best here?"&gt;
- Options object: `pay({ amount, currency })`
- Plain arguments: `pay(amount, currency)`
&lt;/AskPreview&gt;

&lt;AskMany id="choose-checks" title="Step D: choose the checks" question="Which checks should I run before review?" min="1"&gt;
{% for check in checks %}
- {{ check | capitalize }}
{% endfor %}
&lt;/AskMany&gt;

&lt;AskTabs id="choose-settings" title="Step E: settle the details"&gt;
&lt;Tab header="Rollout" question="How should it roll out?"&gt;
All at once (Recommended), or gradually
&lt;/Tab&gt;

&lt;Tab header="Docs" question="Which docs need updating?" multi="true"&gt;
README, or the changelog, or the API reference
&lt;/Tab&gt;
&lt;/AskTabs&gt;

&lt;PlanMode id="approve-plan" title="Step F: get the plan approved"&gt;
- The answers from steps A to E
- The checks you will run, and in what order
&lt;/PlanMode&gt;

&lt;Subagents use="when" max="{{ max_subagents }}" when="the work splits into independent parts, or needs broad searching" not_when="the steps depend on each other" /&gt;

&lt;SubagentFlow id="build-flow" title="Step G: build it" name="research, build, review"&gt;
&lt;Stage n="1" title="Research" id="research" parallel="{{ max_subagents }}" output="Short findings with file paths, and no changes to any file" done="you could explain the change, with evidence for each claim"&gt;
Find the code this feature touches.
&lt;/Stage&gt;

&lt;Stage n="2" title="Build" id="build" output="The changes made, and how they were checked" done="the code is changed and the tests pass"&gt;
Make the change the user chose in step B.
&lt;/Stage&gt;

&lt;Stage n="3" title="Review" id="review" agent="a fresh subagent that did not write the code" output="Real problems, each with a file, a line and why it matters" done="each problem is fixed, or you have explained why it stays"&gt;
Look for bugs in the changes.
&lt;/Stage&gt;
&lt;/SubagentFlow&gt;

&lt;ParallelWork id="split-work" title="Step G2: split the build, if it allows" max="{{ max_subagents }}" /&gt;

&lt;Backoff timeout="{{ timeout }}" retries="{{ retries }}" base="2s" factor="2" limit="30s" on="timeouts, network errors and rate limits" /&gt;

## Checks to run
&lt;Anchor id="checks" /&gt;

{# A loop that calls a macro defined above. #}
{% for check in checks %}
{{ check_row(check, loop.index) }}
{% endfor %}

&lt;Flow id="ship-flow" name="ship it"&gt;
&lt;Step n="1" title="Confirm" id="confirm" ask="Is this ready to ship?" subagent="Do not ask. Report that it is ready, with your evidence."&gt;Summarize what changed and what you checked.&lt;/Step&gt;

&lt;Step n="2" title="Ship" id="ship" subagent="Do not ship. Only the agent that started you does that."&gt;Open the pull request.&lt;/Step&gt;
&lt;/Flow&gt;

&lt;AskConfirm id="delete-branch" title="Step H: clean up" question="Delete the merged feature branch?" /&gt;

&lt;OutputFormat&gt;
Done: what changed
Checked: what you ran and the result
Next: what remains, or "nothing"
&lt;/OutputFormat&gt;

&lt;DynamicSection id="progress" title="Progress" update="after each step above" keep="the current step, and anything blocking it"&gt;Not started.&lt;/DynamicSection&gt;

&lt;DynamicSection id="changelog" title="Release notes" file="RELEASE_NOTES.md" update="whenever the plan changes" /&gt;

{# Some rules come from RichMarkdown, and one is used alone, with extra advice. #}
&lt;RichMarkdown id="formatting" title="How to format your replies" surface="{{ surface }}" only="code,shell,diff,table,checklist,callout,tree,diagram,image,details" /&gt;

&lt;Render kind="fileref" surface="{{ surface }}"&gt;In this demo, cite the checkout code this way in every review finding.&lt;/Render&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Included with <code>{% include "partials/house-style.md" %}</code>.</p> .agent/template/partials/house-style.md<pre><code>House style for {{ project }}: small commits, plain language, and a test for every fix.
</code></pre> <p>Used as <code>&lt;DemoBadge label="..."&gt;...&lt;/DemoBadge&gt;</code>. Props become variables, and the tag's content becomes <code>children</code>.</p> .agent/template/components/DemoBadge.md<pre><code>&gt; **{{ label | default("Note") | upper }}:** {{ children | trim }}
</code></pre>
